<title>UK: Titanium slag ship still aground in St. Lawrence.</title>
<headline>Titanium slag ship still aground in St. Lawrence.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The bulk carrier Utviken, carrying a cargo of titanium slag, is still still aground in the St. Lawrence Seaway, Quebec, and its cargo is to be lightened, Lloyd's Shipping Intelligence Service said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The 30,052-dwt Bahamas flag ship has been damaged and has 71,000 tonnes of fuel on board. It was en route from Richards Bay, South Africa, to Detroit.</p>
</text>
